  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 9.3.3 - Fix binary content detection for Office documents\nBUGFIX: .xlsx, .docx, .pptx files no longer corrupted when downloaded\n   - Root cause: \"xml\" substring in \"openxmlformats\" MIME type triggered text detection\n   - Now uses precise MIME type matching instead of substring matching\nNEW: Comprehensive known-binary MIME type registry (100+ types)\n   - Office documents, PDFs, archives, images, audio, video, fonts, and more\nNEW: ForceBinary option to override content type detection\n   - CurlRequestBuilder.AsBinary() - force binary mode\n   - CurlRequestBuilder.WithBinaryContentType() - register custom binary MIME types\n   - CurlRequestBuilder.WithTextContentType() - register custom text MIME types\nFIXED: Null Content-Type now defaults to binary (previously defaulted to text)\nFrameworks: netstandard2.0, net472, net48, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0\nSponsored by IronSoftware\n\nDocumentation: https://jacob-mellor.github.io/curl-dot-net/\nRepository: https://github.com/jacob-mellor/curl-dot-net\nNuGet: https://www.nuget.org/packages/CurlDotNet/",
